                        "glosses": [
                            "Like a babe; childish; babyish."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "55dd997a-c1cb-4a1a-b4f0-eee17a7d17c4",
                                "sense_id": "f2e81369-7ad7-3dc0-966b-33f539843c40",
                                "text": "Spoons, you know, are to feed us with weak and thin food, even with that which best suiteth with weak stomachs, or with a babish temper."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d8fccbcd-c30f-47b3-aefb-510cc6b340e1",
                                "sense_id": "f2e81369-7ad7-3dc0-966b-33f539843c40",
                                "text": "For, if a young gentleman be demure and still of mature, they say he is simple and lacketh wit; if he be bashful, and will soon blush, they call him a babish and ill brought up thing;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6eae580-12db-45e9-a9af-ccc0d2f78757",
                                "sense_id": "f2e81369-7ad7-3dc0-966b-33f539843c40",
                                "text": "The rot of schools Of medieval time Is Christmas, a pleasing mime To babish minds, Its tinsel blinds The eyes of Thought, 'Tis rot, rot, all rot; And not for me !"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
